pr_body:
This change adds profiling statistics for the dfs phase that look like the following:

```
{
    ...
    "dfs" : {
        "statistics" : {
            "type" : "statistics",
            "description" : "collect term statistics",
            "time_in_nanos" : 236955,
            "breakdown" : {
                "term_statistics" : 4815,
                "collection_statistics" : 27081,
                "collection_statistics_count" : 1,
                "create_weight" : 153278,
                "term_statistics_count" : 1,
                "rewrite_count" : 0,
                "create_weight_count" : 1,
                "rewrite" : 0
            }
        }
    }
    ...
}
```

This change also adds documentation for both the above dfs phase profiling and kNN profiling.

Closes https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/89713

comments:
A sketch of how the new section might look look:

```
{
  "dfs": {
    "query": {
      "type": "KnnVectorQuery",
      "description": "KnnVectorQuery:vector[0.1, 0.2, ...][10]",
      "time_in_nanos": "3801935",
      "breakdown": {...}
    }
  },
  "searches": [ ... ],
  "aggregations": [ ... ],
  "fetch": { ... },
}
```

I used the general name `query` to indicate any query run in the DFS phase. Currently we only ever run kNN queries, so it could make sense to use `knn` as a key instead.
